---
title: Remizidae
---
# Remizidae

Remizidae is a small Old World family of tiny, tit-like songbirds, of which the
[[penduline-tit]] is the best known. The structures the males make are among the
most elaborate produced by any songbird: a thick-walled purse of plant down and
spider silk, felted rather than plaited, and suspended from a drooping twig. The
family is not closely related to the true tits despite the resemblance.
